Chosen global rule for clip constants: empirical p99
Reason: normalization constants are upper clipping scales in value/constant normalization,
and with a dataset of more than 30,000 league matches, p99 remains robust while preserving more
legitimate upper-tail variation than p95. The same less-strict philosophy is used for Elo by
recommending p01/p99 bounds instead of p02/p98.

